mh2lm: preserve framebuffer contents during display-off (0127)

The 0113 lock-screen charger wake reaches the standard IOPM notification
chain and real CoreBrightness backlight control, but it resumes to a partial
lock screen. SweetFramebuffer currently responds to RequestPowerChange(0) by
mutating every physical framebuffer pixel to black. On power-on it can replay
only the latest 4-layer CoreAnimation swap, which need not include the clock
layer, leaving the erased region black.

Add an opt-in `sweetfbpreserveoff=1` experiment. It leaves the framebuffer
contents intact while display-off is active, but retains the normal power
request, vsync notifications, pending-swap behavior, and AppleARMBacklight
path. On MH2LM, CoreBrightness already drives real panel brightness to its
lowest safe level through DCS 0x51, so the screen can be physically black
without destroying the last complete CPU-composited frame.

The default remains the existing fade/clear behavior. This patch adds no
shadow buffer, IOSurface retention, compositor state, GPU behavior, PMIC
change, or display power request. It is deliberately an A/B diagnostic before
considering a bounded shadow buffer or a GPU-present backend.

